  "description": "Proposed single-storey rear conservatory extension to the existing dwelling. The development comprises a fully glazed structure with a roof formed in blue self-cleaning, solar control glass and 28mm toughened safety glass framing, providing additional living space, enhancing residential amenity, increasing natural daylight, and improving the connection to the rear garden.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed conservatory, by reason of its depth in combination with the existing rear extension, would not appear subservient to the main dwellinghouse and would not sit comfortably within the existing pattern of development. As such, the proposed development is contrary to:National Planning Policy Framework&nbsp; National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024); Policies D1, D4, D5 and D6 of the London Plan (March 2021); Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 &nbsp;of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham&#39;s Local Plan (September 2024); andThe Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012)",
    "The scale, siting and design of the proposed development would result in a harmful level of overshadowing and introducing a sense of overbearing to neighbouring occupiers, therefore constituting unneighbourly development and contrary to: National Planning Policy Framework National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December 2024); Policy D4 of the London Plan (March 2021); Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 &nbsp;of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham&#39;s Local Plan (September 2024); andThe Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012);"
  ],
